      "writtenOn": "2024-04-04T23:45:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we only need to handle custom implementations here and just forward the rest of these as-is:\n\n```\nswitch(ucsi_command) {\n  /* Custom only because of the idle state. */\n  case UCSI_CMD_PPM_RESET:\n    rv \u003d rts54_reset(dev);\n    break;\n    \n  /* Needed to clear interrupt bits on Connection Indicator. */\n  case UCSI_CMD_ACK_CC_CI:\n    /* Handle acks. Looks like the driver doesn\u0027t do this today. */\n    break;\n    \n  /* All other commands should mostly be passed through as-is. */\n  default:\n    if (get_state(data) \u003d\u003d ST_IDLE) {\n      data_size \u003d ucsi_commands[ucsi_command].command_copy_length;\n      dev-\u003ecmd_buffer[0] \u003d 0xE; /* Cmd */\n      dev-\u003ecmd_buffer[1] \u003d data_size + 2;\n      dev-\u003ecmd_buffer[2] \u003d ucsi_command; /* sub-cmd */\n      memcpy(\u0026dev-\u003ecmd_buffer[3], control-\u003ecommand_specific_data,\n        data_size);\n        \n      rv \u003d rts54_post_command(dev, CMD_PPM_RESET + ucsi_command, dev-\u003ecmd_buffer, data_size + 2, lpm_data_out);\n    } else {\n      rv \u003d -EBUSY;\n    }\n    \n    break;\n}\n\nreturn rv;\n\n```",
      "revId": "b7de6b66c2b33c604f569652b9e3072a90d7ec05",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
